<Base titolo="Privacy policy" percorso={[{ titolo: 'Privacy policy' }]} descrizione="How the Ripetizioni di Analisi website processes personal data: which data it collects, what they are used for and what your rights are." lingua="en" seo={{ soloQuestaLingua: false }}>
  <p class="sopratitolo">Privacy</p>
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="sommario">Which data the website collects, what they are used for and what your rights are. Last updated: 13 November 2026. This is a translation; the Italian version prevails.</p>

  <h2>In short</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The website collects only the data needed to run accounts, purchases and support.</li>
    <li>Your data are <strong>not sold or passed on to third parties</strong>, and we use them for study suggestions and offers by email only with your consent.</li>
    <li>The only external services are the essential technical providers: <strong>Cloudflare</strong>, which hosts the website and the data, <strong>Stripe</strong>, which processes payments for digital products and private lessons, <strong>Paddle</strong>, which handles earlier purchases where it was the reseller, <strong>Google</strong>, which hosts the videos of the video courses and the lesson calendar with Google Meet, and <strong>Resend</strong>, which sends the website’s emails. Each processes the data only to provide its own service.</li>
    <li>Your password is stored in hashed form and cannot be read by anyone, not even by the controller.</li>
    <li>You can ask at any time to see, correct or delete your data.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Data controller</h2>
  <p>Carmine Tornincasa, who can be contacted at <a href="mailto:carminetornincasa98@gmail.com">carminetornincasa98@gmail.com</a>.</p>

  <h2>Which data are processed</h2>
  <p><strong>Account.</strong> For those who create an account, the website stores the name, the email address, the password in hashed form, the unlocked subjects, the registration date and the date of the last login. It also stores the browser and system type of the connected devices (at most two), the channel of the first visit (for example Instagram or Google) and, if you state it when signing up, the courses you attended, are attending or purchased from Carmine. These data are used to run the account, to limit use to three devices, to unlock free subjects for course students and to provide support.</p>
  <p><strong>Study reminders.</strong> If study reminders are enabled, after 3 and 10 days of inactivity the website may remind you of the last topic you studied and the level you reached. It uses your last activity while signed in and the last topic you opened. You can turn off reminders in your settings or using the link in the email.</p>
  <p id="email-studio-offerte"><strong>Free exercises and email offers.</strong> If you declare that you are 18 or older and confirm your consent, we may send you a free exercise in the subject you pick and offer a discount on a related subject after a purchase. We use your subject preference, signup date, study activity and account purchases to choose a relevant message and keep within one promotional email per week. Resend sends these emails on our behalf. We record when consent is granted or withdrawn and the version of the choice. Individual automated sending records are kept for up to 90 days. You can withdraw consent at any time in <a href="/en/account#impostazioni">Email preferences</a> or via the link in the email.</p>
  <p><strong>Forgotten password.</strong> Those who request a new password enter the account email. The website sends a link valid for one hour to that address through the Resend sending service, which receives only the address and the text of the message. To prevent abuse the website counts each day's requests and deletes them after one week.</p>
  <p id="fatturazione-digitale"><strong>Digital purchases.</strong> To invoice a purchase, Carmine collects the first and last name and residential address of the person being billed, including country, city, and postal code and region where applicable. Italian residents also provide their Italian tax code. These details are linked to the order in the restricted billing area. Stripe processes the payment and handles card details according to its <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>. We record the product, amount, payment reference and status, the email address used at checkout, and your choices about the terms and access to the content. These records are used to confirm the order, grant access and handle invoicing, withdrawal and refunds. For earlier purchases from Paddle, the reseller handles the billing details under <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/privacy" rel="noopener">Paddle’s privacy policy</a>.</p>
  <p><strong>Welcome discount.</strong> Whoever creates an account from the bar at the bottom of the website gets a discount on the first purchase of a subject. The website records that the account was created there and the page the sign-up came from; at checkout a personal discount is applied to the eligible order. No emails are sent for this discount.</p>
  <p><strong>Group courses.</strong> Whoever enrols in a group course provides first and last name, email, phone number and, optionally, university, degree course, lecturer, exam date, notes and past exam papers (PDF or photos). These data are used to form the group, to create the course WhatsApp group and to build the syllabus on the exam papers. They are stored on Cloudflare's servers and only the controller can see them; the enrolment confirmation is sent through Resend.</p>
  <p id="fatturazione"><strong>Private lessons.</strong> To book, you provide contact details for the lesson and may include your university and the topics you would like to cover. For the invoice, the site asks for the first and last name and residential address of the person being billed, including country, city, postal code and province or region where applicable. Italian residents also provide their Italian tax code. The billing details are linked to the booking for invoicing and accounting purposes. The lesson is added to the controller's Google Calendar with name, email, phone and topics; Google sends the student the invitation with the Google Meet link. Payment is handled by Stripe, which collects the card data according to its <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>: the website receives only the payment confirmation and the amount. Confirmation, rescheduling and cancellation emails are sent through Resend. To limit bookings left pending, the website keeps a non-reversible fingerprint of the network address of whoever books.</p>
  <p><strong>Invite a friend.</strong> Every account has a personal invite code. Whoever opens an invite link receives for 30 days the technical cookie <code>invito</code> with that code; if they create an account in that period, the site records which account invited them. This is used only to apply the first-purchase discount and to give the inviter a discount when the friend buys a subject; the inviter receives a notice email through Resend, without the friend's name or email. The site records which orders used a discount.</p>
  <p id="orientamento"><strong>Guidance: preview for GM accounts.</strong> During this trial phase, the study tests and university questionnaire, available in Italian, can only be accessed with an account granted the GM permission by the website operator. The account is used to verify access permission. Answers are processed in your browser using fixed rules and are not sent to artificial intelligence services. Unless you ask to keep them, they stay only in the page’s memory and are lost when you reload or close it.</p>
  <p><strong>Keeping answers on this device.</strong> You can request this by choosing to keep answers on this device, using the save and pause command, or using the device storage command on the result page. The initial option is not preselected. Answers, test settings and any result stay in this browser for 30 days after your last activity. Expiry is checked when you reopen the guidance service; the website cannot physically remove the data while your browser is closed. You can remove them with the local deletion button or through your browser settings. The button also stops further automatic local saving until you request it again; it does not delete results saved in your account.</p>
  <p><strong>Saving in your account.</strong> This is a separate choice from keeping answers on the device. Only when you choose to save in your account does the website receive and store on Cloudflare’s servers your answers, result, test type and version, subject and study goal or any university area you selected, together with the save date. The server also recalculates the result using the same fixed rules. These data are linked to your account so that you can reopen the result on another device.</p>
  <p><strong>How long account results are kept.</strong> The website keeps the latest saved result for each subject and the latest university questionnaire for 365 days after the last save. Viewing a result does not renew this period. Once it expires, the account no longer returns the result; it is removed from the operational database by the access check or by the cleanup scheduled every hour.</p>
  <p><strong>Deleting results.</strong> You can delete them before expiry in the guidance section of your GM account. Deletion removes them from the operational database and also removes the corresponding draft in the browser you are using, if present. If the browser prevents its removal, the website tells you. Copies on other devices and drafts of new attempts remain separate and can be deleted in the relevant browser. If your GM permission is revoked, you can request a copy or deletion of your results using the controller’s contact details in this policy. Closing your account also removes its saved results. Cloudflare’s technical recovery copies follow a separate cycle, with a <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/api/sqlite-storage-api/#pitr-point-in-time-recovery-api" rel="noopener">recovery window of up to 30 days</a>; deleting records from the operational database does not immediately remove those copies.</p>
  <p><strong>Use of answers and results.</strong> They are used to return exercises to revisit and study materials to consult, or a summary of your declared interests and areas of study to explore. They are not used to send offers or emails, make admission decisions, or determine prices or purchases. The result provides suggestions that you can freely consider and does not make decisions with legal effects on you. The website’s other services continue to follow the purposes and conditions described in their respective sections of this policy.</p>
  <p><strong>Formula sheets.</strong> Formula sheets can be read without an account; downloading the PDF requires an account, even with no purchases.</p>
  <p><strong>Browsing.</strong> The website counts page visits in aggregate form (day and section visited). To count the distinct visitors of each day it computes a non-reversible fingerprint from the date, the network address and the browser type; the fingerprint does not identify the person, and the network address is not stored. Fingerprints are deleted after 200 days.</p>
  <p><strong>Pi assistant.</strong> Those who use the assistant send their question, the text of the part of the page they are reading and, optionally, a photo of an exercise. This content is processed by Cloudflare's artificial intelligence service (Workers AI) only to generate the answer. The website does not keep conversations or photos: it only keeps the number of messages sent each day, to apply the daily limit. For those who use Pi without an account, the count uses a non-reversible fingerprint of the network address and the browser. The conversation is saved for 24 hours only in your browser and never reaches the website.</p>
  <p><strong>Exam compatibility check.</strong> The compatibility check (Italian pages only) receives the text of an exam paper or course syllabus (photos, a PDF turned into images in the browser, or typed text) and, optionally, the name of the university. Images are processed by Cloudflare's AI service (Workers AI) to transcribe the exercises or syllabus topics. The site keeps, without name, email or account, the document sent (page images and text), the result of the comparison, the subject and the university given, to improve the material and prepare similar exercises. Images may contain data written on the sheet (such as a name or student number): it is best to cover them before taking the photo. To apply the daily limit it counts the checks made by each account or, without an account, by a non-reversible fingerprint of the network address and browser. Recent results are saved only in your browser.</p>
  <p><strong>Video courses.</strong> The videos and PDFs of the video courses are stored in Google Drive folders. Those who purchased a video course request access to the folder with their Google account, and Carmine sees the email address used for the request. Google processes these data according to its <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>.</p>
  <p><strong>Contacts.</strong> If you write to Carmine on WhatsApp or by email, the message is used only to reply to you.</p>

  <h2>Where data are stored and how they are protected</h2>
  <p>Account and purchase data are stored on the servers of Cloudflare, which hosts the website. Communications with the website are encrypted (HTTPS), the password is stored only in hashed form, and only the controller can access student data, with a private password.</p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>The website uses only technical cookies: <code>sessione</code> keeps you logged in, <code>dispositivo</code> recognises the device connected to the account, <code>fonte</code> remembers the channel of the first visit for 90 days, <code>invito</code> keeps the code of an opened invite link for 30 days to apply the discount. There are no profiling cookies and no third-party cookies for browsing. Some reading preferences, such as whether the contents panel is open or closed, are stored only on the device and never leave the browser. Stripe may set cookies necessary to process payments. For earlier purchases handled by Paddle, its own portal may use cookies for support or refunds.</p>
  {MISURAZIONE_ATTIVA && <p><strong>Measurement cookies (only with your consent).</strong> The website uses Google tools (Google Ads and Google Analytics) to count how many people arrive from ads and searches and how many of them create an account, book a lesson, join a course or buy a subject. Until you accept from the banner, Google sets no cookies and receives only anonymous signals without identifiers. If you accept, Google sets its own cookies (for example <code>_ga</code>, <code>_gcl_au</code>) to recognise the browser and attribute the conversion to the ad, and at the time of a purchase the website sends Google the account email in hashed, unreadable form, to count conversions more accurately. Google processes these data according to its <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>. You can change your choice at any time from <a href="#" data-consenso-apri>this link</a>.</p>}

  <h2>Legal basis and retention</h2>
  <p>The processing of account, purchase and support data is based on the performance of a contract (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR); aggregate statistics are based on the legitimate interest in running the website. Email offers and study suggestions are based on consent (Article 6(1)(a) GDPR). Account data are kept for as long as the service is active, so that access can be restored to those who purchased a subject, or until you ask for their deletion. Billing records for paid lessons and digital orders are kept to comply with tax and accounting obligations (Article 6(1)(c) GDPR) for the period required by law.</p>
  <p>Saving guidance results in your account is an optional service that you expressly request: the processing necessary to provide it is based on Article 6(1)(b) of the <a href="https://www.garanteprivacy.it/il-testo-del-regolamento" rel="noopener">GDPR</a>. Browser storage is the technical function you request to resume the test on the same device. You can take the tests without enabling either form of storage and without consenting to promotional emails. The specific retention periods of 30 days in the browser and 365 days in the account described above apply to guidance data even if the account remains active for longer.</p>
  <p><strong>Minors and guidance.</strong> The <a href="https://www.garanteprivacy.it/temi/minori" rel="noopener">Italian age threshold of 14</a> concerns consent to data processing for online services offered directly to minors when consent is the legal basis for processing. National rules on the validity of contracts entered into by minors continue to apply, including to the account.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can at any time request access to, rectification or erasure of your data by writing to the controller's address. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the Italian Data Protection Authority (Garante per la protezione dei dati personali).</p>
  <p>For guidance data, where the GDPR provides for these rights, you can also request restriction of processing and data portability: receiving the data you provided in a structured, machine-readable format so that you can transfer them to another service. You can send these requests to the same controller’s address.</p>
</Base>
